COLORS IN CAR CABLES
→ 629.28 → Automotive Technology

          [ CAR ]

     |        |        |        |        |        |
    RED     BLACK    YELLOW    BLUE    GREEN    WHITE
     |        |        |        |        |        |
    +12V     GND      ACC      REM      SIG      LGT

Red     = Battery positive  (type: power)
Black   = Chassis ground    (type: return / negative)
Yellow  = Accessories + ignition  (type: switched power)
Blue    = Remote accessories      (type: switched / signal)
Green   = Sensors + control       (type: signal / low-current)
White   = Lighting circuits       (type: load / illumination)

Fundamentals
- Typical system: 12 V DC
- Red = positive feed from battery
- Black = ground / negative return
- Colors are a common convention, not a universal standard
- Always confirm with the vehicle-specific wiring diagram
